& [Fold01_IdentityBoundary] asks what identity is being named
  + [probe] separate evidence type identity, evidence variant identity, physical acquisition identity, receipt representation identity, issuer identity, and world-state identity
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence identifies a closed vocabulary of evidence grades, not a consistency state of the world
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual identifies a lineage-dependent relation between two actual complete acquisitions
  + the variant contains no acquisition identities and therefore cannot create that lineage by construction
  + TopologyReceipt.consistency_evidence names the grade a later issuer must support, not the issuer or support itself
  + receipt_profile identifies the current receipt representation and validation contract
  + scanner_profile continues to identify the unchanged prospective scanner contract
  + OsSnapshotProven identifies a reserved evidence kind but has no current receipt representation capable of carrying its provenance
  + [edge_equal_supplied_digest_pair] is insufficient because operand equality is not actual acquisition identity
  + [edge_same_physical_tree_at_one_instant] is insufficient because neither an instant nor atomic snapshot is observed by two ordinary walks
  + [finding] every identity retains one role and no serialized enum value becomes an issuer, observation, or state fact

& [Fold02_LinguisticTruth] asks what each public word may honestly imply
  + [probe] compare quiescent, stable, unchanged, snapshot, atomic, repeated, inventory, equal, and evidence
  + quiescent implies an absence or controlled cessation of relevant change that ordinary repeated walks cannot prove
  + stable and unchanged imply a temporal continuity stronger than endpoint equality
  + snapshot and atomic imply one indivisible observation boundary or platform primitive
  + repeated means two actual acquisitions and therefore cannot be inferred from duplicated or caller-supplied values
  + inventory means complete acquisition under a separately authorized producer contract, not any arbitrary digest carrier
  + equal means the two exact canonical committed inventory subjects compare equal within one common scope
  + evidence means inspectable support whose admissibility and lineage must still be checked by its consumer
  + NonAtomic explicitly denies the snapshot, transaction, lock, and uninterrupted-interval implications
  + [edge_change_then_restore] remains compatible with NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + [edge_change_after_second_walk] remains compatible with NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + [edge_external_writer] remains compatible even if a supervisor accounts for its own processes
  + [finding] the replacement is the weakest honest current public machine phrase and preserves explicit nonclaims

& [Fold03_AdversarialProvenance] asks how evidence could be laundered
  + [probe_fabricated_form] caller constructs a valid TopologyReceipt and selects the admitted enum
    - structural validation succeeds only as form validation; documentation and absent issuer API deny physical proof
  + [probe_duplicated_carrier] caller supplies the same reconciliation carrier twice
    - pure reconciliation may report Equal but no current conversion to repeated acquisition evidence exists
  + [probe_old_json] caller submits consistency plus quiescent_double_inventory
    - deny through strict unknown-field and closed-enum decoding
  + [probe_dual_fields] caller submits both consistency and consistency_evidence
    - deny because consistency remains unknown under deny_unknown_fields
  + [probe_snapshot_token] caller selects os_snapshot_proven without snapshot lineage
    - structural enum validation alone passes, but TopologyReceipt semantic validation rejects at consistency_evidence
  + [probe_old_profile_new_field] caller changes only the field while retaining receipt 0.2
    - exact receipt profile rejects
  + [probe_new_profile_old_token] caller changes only the profile
    - strict enum decoding rejects before semantic validation
  + [probe_historical_artifact] preserved proof contains the old token
    - historical bytes remain inspectable but are never automatically decoded as current authority
  + [finding] strict replacement, no conversion, and issuer absence block every examined provenance-laundering route

& [Fold04_DataOwnershipAndCardinality] asks what the two pure modules can own and prove
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence is one closed Copy value with exactly two variants
  + TopologyReceipt owns exactly one consistency_evidence value in the same semantic position as the removed field
  + the enum owns no acquisition record, snapshot record, issuer signature, clock, or policy proof
  + the receipt retains every existing scalar, identity, limits, digest, nonce, and tick field unchanged
  + semantic validation borrows the receipt and returns no newly owned proof object
  + successful validation does not enrich, replace, sign, or persist the caller-owned receipt
  + failure releases one bounded atomic TopologyFormFault and no partial receipt
  + [edge_zero_evidence_fields] strict deserialization rejects missing consistency_evidence
  + [edge_two_evidence_fields] impossible in the Rust struct and rejected in old-plus-new JSON
  + [edge_extra_variant] impossible without source and enum change
  + [finding] representation cardinality stays one evidence label while proof cardinality remains zero inside this revision

& [Fold05_FaultAndControlFlow] asks whether every invalid form fails at the right boundary
  + malformed JSON, unknown legacy field, missing new field, dual fields, and old token are Json faults
  + exact structural decode occurs before semantic receipt validation
  + receipt profile 0.2 reaches a bounded Receipt fault at receipt_profile only when otherwise decodable current JSON is constructed
  + OsSnapshotProven reaches a bounded Receipt fault at consistency_evidence
  + NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual proceeds to all unchanged receipt invariants in their established deterministic order
  + evidence grade failure never falls back to a weaker or older value
  + no fault carries a receipt, acquisition, reconciliation result, physical observation, or partial success
  + a failed validation does not mutate caller data or global state
  + [edge_snapshot_plus_other_invalid_field] deterministic existing validation order remains canonical; tests target an otherwise valid snapshot receipt for exact attribution
  + [edge_legacy_profile_raw_json] malformed representation is Json; semantically wrong current-shaped profile is Receipt, preserving parser-versus-validator separation
  + [finding] fault taxonomy stays atomic and the revision introduces no repair or migration control flow

& [Fold06_EffectAndThreatSurface] asks what execution can observe or change
  + enum serialization and deserialization operate only on supplied in-memory values
  + ValidatePhase3 for InventoryConsistencyEvidence performs closed structural validation only
  + TopologyReceipt validation reads supplied fields and applies bounded pure predicates
  + no physical acquisition, filesystem access, Windows API, process observation, clock read, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, fixture, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion is invoked
  + no unsafe block, handle, pointer, external dependency, thread, lock, callback, or effect-bearing constructor is added
  + Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock remain byte identical
  + [edge_claim_by_type_name] machine vocabulary can still mislead a consumer; direct rustdoc nonclaims and static vocabulary tests are therefore required security controls
  + [edge_denial_of_service] no new variable-sized payload or recursion is introduced
  + [edge_false_assurance] reserved snapshot value is fail-closed at the only revised receipt consumer
  + [finding] the slice reduces semantic threat surface while leaving operational effect surface exactly zero

& [Fold07_EvolutionAndCompatibility] asks how the replacement behaves under future work
  + machine forms 0.1, topology forms 0.2, and receipt 0.2 fail current exact-profile validation rather than migrate
  + compiled callers using ConsistencyClass or consistency fail at compile time and must make a conscious semantic change
  + serialized callers using old field or token fail at decode and must make a conscious schema change
  + OsSnapshotProven remains available for future source expansion but current receipt rejection prevents premature use
  + future snapshot support requires exact provenance fields, primitive, producer, issuer, proof, profile revision, and replacement authority
  + future supervisor-quiesced evidence requires a newly named variant and explicit external-writer nonclaims
  + future M2C may consume pure reconciliation only as a subordinate equality edge beside two actual acquisition lineages
  + future receipt issuance must remain distinct from public form construction and validation
  + rollback restores two modules and their tests without migration because no live producer or persisted consumer exists
  + [edge_historical_proof] retained old artifacts continue to mean what their then-current signatures declared; no retroactive reinterpretation occurs
  + [finding] compatibility fails closed at compile, decode, and profile boundaries while history remains immutable

& [CrossFoldConvergence] is explicit
  + Fold01 role-separated identity supports Fold02 precise language and prevents Fold03 provenance laundering
  + Fold02 non-atomic wording makes Fold06 absence of physical effects visible in the machine token itself
  + Fold03 strict replacement is implementable with Fold04 one-field cardinality and Fold05 parser-versus-validator faults
  + Fold04 zero embedded provenance explains why Fold03 issuer absence and snapshot rejection are mandatory
  + Fold05 atomic failure preserves Fold01 identity boundaries instead of coercing one grade into another
  + Fold06 zero effects keeps Fold04 ownership pure and forces future physical meaning into Fold07 separate authority
  + Fold07 fail-closed evolution protects every prohibition established by Folds01 through 06

